“Bulls; trees; cows; oxen;
horse; bronze goblet; she-jackal; water-pot;
lotus pond; uncookable rice; sandalwood;
pumpkins sink; stones float;

frogs swallow black cobras;
golden swans surround a crow;
the wolf trembles for fear of the sheep.”

For the second time I take refuge in the Buddha,
for the second time I take refuge in the Teaching,
for the second time I take refuge in the Saṅgha.

For the third time I take refuge in the Buddha,
for the third time I take refuge in the Teaching,
for the third time I take refuge in the Saṅgha.
